WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.520
Located in a narrow water inlet that separates
Europe and Asia, Istanbul is a city rooted

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.450
in the most influential corners of history.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.990
Few cities can boast of having a past like
theirs.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:33.070
An ancient city once known as Byzantium, then
Constantinople, Istanbul was once the capital

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.550
of three great empires: the Roman empire of
the East, the Byzantine Empire, and the Ottoman

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.300
Empire.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.910
Places like Saint Sophia, the Blue Mosque,
and the Grand Bazaar are legacies from that

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.910
era.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:55.460
But, folks… wait just a second… because
all that is in the… past.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:01.969
Nowadays, Istanbul is a lively city that hosts
more than 15 million inhabitants.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:03.309
The largest city in all of Europe.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:05.780
And an important economic enclave.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.680
1 out of every 3 dollars of Turkey's GDP is
generated here.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.320
And even though it barely hosts a fifth of
the country’s entire population, the Turkish

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.710
government gets about half of all its tax
revenue from Istanbul.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:24.520
So we’re talking about Turkey’s true economic
engine.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.620
A growing financial, logistical, commercial,
and of course… touristic hub.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.750
Istanbul attracts 13.4 million foreign visitors
in 2018.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.750
Daily Sabah)

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.290
However, folks, in recent years, Istanbul
has begun to be well-known for a different

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.290
kind of tourism.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.560
A very, very special tourism model.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.170
As special as it is controversial.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:47.140
Have you ever heard of medical tourism?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.960
Listen up.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:57.020
(A HIGH-FLYING TOUR)

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.830
Every year, hundreds of millions of people
travel abroad to experience a new culture

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:06.090
and enjoy the sun, the beach, the mountains,
or famous art and architecture.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:12.730
However, folks, another type of unconventional
but highly coveted tourism has recently gained

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.040
popularity: medical tourism.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.400
That is, traveling to another country to visit
its monuments, beaches and, in passing, fixing

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.790
anything they may need fixed.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.770
“They usually come for three days.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:30.660
We offer them shopping or skiing tours, they
get well and have a short vacation,” said

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.780
Kazim Devranoglu, the medical head of Dunyagoz
Group)

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.190
And folks, I can already tell you that for
many governments, starting with Turkey’s,

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.320
this is a priority.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.320
Of course...

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.420
At this point we need to answer two questions
that many of you may be asking.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.920
The first is... why go to another country
in search of medical treatment?

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.550
Well... this has three very, very clear answers.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.919
The first... is the price.

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:53.920
Of course, if you have to get a medical procedure
that isn’t covered by your health insurance...

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.410
price matters.... a lot.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.100
For example, some interventions and treatments
are much cheaper in Istanbul than they are

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.220
in the United States.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.920
And when I say cheaper I mean much cheaper.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.190
50, 60, 70 and even more than 80% cheaper.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.210
The second reason has to do with waiting lists.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:17.419
Yes, you may be covered by your health insurance
or social security, but... what about waiting

00:03:17.419 --> 00:03:18.419
lists?

00:03:18.419 --> 00:03:21.860
In public health systems such as those found
in Spain or the United Kingdom, it’s very

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.080
common to have waiting lists... which are
quite long.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.940
[Which means you have to wait a long time
for your turn.]

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:34.070
But of course, what happens if you can’t
or don’t want to wait?

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.920
Then you need to find something on your own.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.480
And in that scenario, the big international
medical centers... don’t really have waiting

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.729
lists, or they’re much shorter.

00:03:43.729 --> 00:03:50.130
The waiting time for a knee surgery in a Western
Country is 18 moths, but is only two weeks

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.500
at most in Turkey.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.350
Emre A. Kodan, Chairman of the Istanbul International
Health Tourism Association.)

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:03.410
Check out how the number of British medical
tourists has grown:

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.930
And the third reason is quality.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.420
Yes, yes, you heard that right.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.870
When a place specializes in a particular treatment
and has many patients, it tends to be better.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:18.290
Surely you all know about Houston’s Texas
Medical Center, which serves about 10 million

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.500
patients every year, and is one of the leading
medical centers on the planet.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.231
In the end, these places have so many patients
and so many resources that not only are they

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:31.540
very good at their job, they also become engines
of medical research and innovation.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.090
But we said that we had two questions.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.510
We already answered the first one.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.860
So what’s the second?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.910
The other question is, why, exactly, is this
such an important activity for a country?

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.490
Why would a government want to promote this
type of activity?

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.800
Become a kind of International Health Care
Center.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.670
What could that bring to a country?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:57.620
Well, folks...

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.620
Think about it.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:02.070
Along with the traditional jobs that tourism
creates, for example in the hotel industry

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:07.630
– waiters or cooks – medical tourism helps
create a lot of highly qualified and well-paid

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.630
jobs:

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:25.780
Doctors, surgeons, nurses, laboratory personnel,
medical device suppliers, etc., etc.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:29.930
Due to the billing levels and the type of
activity generated, medical tourism is like

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.420
the Rolex of tourism.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:35.780
And on top of that, it doesn’t have the
problem of seasonality, unlike holiday tourism,

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.310
which tends to concentrate within just a few
months, usually during the summer.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.500
And it’s precisely these reasons that have
prompted the Turkish government to place great

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.780
hope in medical tourism.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.780
A lot of hope...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.930
And a lot of money, in the form of incentives:
fewer taxes, financing, aid, etc., etc.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.690
“I believe the city hospitals will become
the focal points of health tourism.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:51.690
We are setting up special units in the city
hospitals to specifically serve foreign patients,”

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:52.690
Turkish Health Minister Fahrettin Koca)

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:53.690
And, you know what?

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.820
In a way, it makes a lot of sense.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.590
Allow me to explain.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.630
If Turkey is already a touristic power—
it has hotels, infrastructure, all kinds of

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:07.200
services, a lot of cultural attractions, and
places like Istanbul are only 2 or 3 hours

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.830
by plane from the main cities of Europe and
the East—

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.210
Why not take advantage?

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:20.460
Well, folks... so it was said and done.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:27.400
Turkey attracted nearly 1 million health tourists
in 2018, industry official says: Daily Sabah)

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:32.990
And as I mentioned, this type of tourism leaves
much more money in a country’s pockets...

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.090
than pure holiday tourism.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:38.850
In 2018, medical tourists left more than 2
billion dollars in Turkey.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.639
Thus, Turkey is already the third-largest
market in the world in terms of medical and

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:43.639
health tourism.

00:06:43.639 --> 00:06:47.900
It stands only behind the United States and
South Korea.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:53.580
Folks, medical tourism in Turkey has multiplied
by more than 10 in the last decade.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.630
Just in 2008, they welcomed 75,000 people.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:03.010
In other words, the industry is skyrocketing.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:06.810
Turkey’s medical tourism industry boosts
visitor numbers.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:10.720
When Turkey’s traditional tourism industry
dried up, the country turned to its medical

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.060
sector to attract a new wave of visitors.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.060
Business Destinations)

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.220
Of course, all this is just the beginning
of what the government expects.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:22.740
The goal is generate 5 times as much income
from medical tourism five times by 2023, greatly

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.360
exceeding the 10 billion dollar barrier.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:30.960
And, some within the government and the private
sector are even more ambitious.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.830
Their goal is 20 billion dollars.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:38.780
A huge business that also gives the country
a large foreign currency inflow.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:42.570
Dental care, dentistry, cosmetic surgery,
fertility treatment, cardiovascular interventions,

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.910
transplants, oncological treatments...

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:50.380
Turkey – and particularly Istanbul – wants
to become a world leader in international

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.610
medical tourism.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:58.540
And in one way or another, this will be very
good for all of us.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.040
Why?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.050
Listen up.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.060
(THE CLUSTER)

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:11.580
Folks, Istanbul is quickly becoming the world
leader in several medical specialties: from

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.960
ophthalmology to knee care and hair transplants.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.270
In some of these fields, it’s already number
1 on the entire planet.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.600
And it’s that way because of price... and
innovation.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:21.949
Yes, you heard that right.

00:08:21.949 --> 00:08:26.810
It has to do with a logical and well-known
market process: Cluster creation.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:32.650
Allow me to explain.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:36.690
This happens when a site specializes in an
activity and many competitors engage in the

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:37.690
same activity.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:41.950
This causes everything in the area to somehow
begin to revolve around that industry: the

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.760
number of suppliers that compete with each
other multiplies; public administrations begin

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:50.320
to facilitate things for this increasingly
influential industry; universities work with

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.820
these companies, etc., etc.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:59.990
That, folks, creates a more dynamic ecosystem
and multiplies its innovation capacity.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:08.589
In other words, so to speak, Istanbul is becoming
the Silicon Valley of cataracts and hair transplants.

00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:09.680
For whomever may want them.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.990
All this may sound like a joke...

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:13.089
But it isn’t.

00:09:13.089 --> 00:09:15.310
The city of Bosphorus already has hundreds
– you heard that right, hundreds – of

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.190
clinics that specialize in this type of activity.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.770
In many cases, we’re talking about very
new clinics with very advanced treatments.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:28.140
And it’s estimated that by 2025, these types
of interventions will move tens and tens of

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:29.140
billions worldwide.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:34.990
Anyway, I think we can now understand news
like this better:

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:39.250
The global medical tourism market size is
expected to reach USD 179.6 billion by 2026,

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:44.320
according to a new report by Grand View Research,
Inc., registering a 21.9% CAGR during the

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:45.320
forecast period.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.320
Grand View Research)

